# autotune-progress: Auto Tune v2 (issue #190) captured at its ONLY provisional
# correction.
#
# Same trigger as `autotune` (APP 6, "Auto Tune" -> main_screen_action(ACTION_ATUNE)),
# but here scenario_settle arms a TEST-ONLY CW tone sample (mocks/mock_cw_tune.c:
# 35 Hz above the configured pitch, mark/noise 20) because the bank cannot compile
# src/cw.cpp (liquid-dsp + the audio thread) and fabricating an RSSI would be
# faking the production path. The three fresh, stable, valid frames of COLLECT
# make the core decide one correction of +35 Hz in CW; the dial steps there once
# and the session goes on to VERIFY.
#
# What the fixture *means*: in v2 there is no sweep and no progress bar - the
# "progress" is a single correction of at most +/-300 Hz - and the capture is that
# instant (the corrected dial with the session still running). scenario_settle
# fails if the dial does not land exactly on the correction or if the session had
# already ended, so a second correction or a silent sweep cannot pass unnoticed.

name autotune-progress
screen autotune-progress

seed 20

frequency_hz 14074000
tx_frequency_hz 14074000
fft_width_hz 384000

mode cw
vfo A
agc auto

split false
att false
pre false
atu false
ant 1

smeter_db -73

battery_v 12.1
external_v 13.8
battery_cap 76
charging false

rxtx rx
